# Commercial Packages & Modular Architecture

See [COMMERCIAL_PACKAGES.md](../../COMMERCIAL_PACKAGES.md).

## Rules

1. Build as modular SaaS — customers pay only for licensed modules.
2. Package resolution maps `subscriptions.plan_key`: starter, growth→professional, business, enterprise.
3. Gate features with `is_tenant_module_enabled()` — never expose unlicensed capabilities.
4. Tenant isolation mandatory — no cross-tenant module or usage data.
5. Feature flags: enabled, disabled, trial, beta, deprecated, enterprise_only.
6. Routes: `/app/settings/billing`, `/app/settings/modules` (spec `/admin/*`).
7. i18n: `customerApp.commercialPackages.*`, `platform.commercialPackages.*` in en/no/sv/da.
8. Integrates existing `plans`, `subscriptions`, and License Center — do not duplicate payment logic.

## Tables

`subscription_packages` · `tenant_modules` · `tenant_usage_metrics`

## Billing reference page

`/app/settings/billing` is the Customer APP billing reference implementation:

- Canonical width via `lib/design/app-layout.ts` (`AppLayoutClasses`)
- View model: `lib/commercial-packages/billing-view-model.ts`
- Labels: `lib/commercial-packages/billing-labels.ts`
- No fake billing data, no raw feature keys, no dead CTAs
- Preview visual QA required before merge; do not treat green unit tests alone as sufficient
